  {
   "kind": "linkedin-post",
   "text": "Some of the biggest companies in tech ranked their staff by how much AI they used. Meta had a leaderboard with titles like \"Token Legend\". Amazon had KiroRank. Staff set AI agents running on unnecessary tasks to climb them, and both boards came down.\n\nWhen one company halved its AI usage target instead, most of the junk vanished and its sales staff sold 7% more.\n\nWhatever you count, people learn to produce. If you're counting how much AI your people use, you're counting rat tails.\n\nThe full deep dive is at makeyourmindup.ai."
  },
